---
import SectionRibbon from "@/components/SectionRibbon/index.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/base.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | PDFvise"
  description="PDFvise processes PDF files in your browser. Files are not uploaded, and the site does not ask you to create an account."
>
  <SectionRibbon
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="PDFvise keeps PDF work on your computer."
  />
  <div class="container" style="padding: calc(3 * var(--pico-spacing)) 0;">
    <p>
      PDFvise, at <a href="https://pdfvise.com">https://pdfvise.com</a>, is a set
      of PDF tools that run in your browser. This policy describes that
      practice.
    </p>
    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <p>
      PDF files you open stay in your browser. The tools read and write them on
      your device. PDFvise does not upload those files, does not keep a copy,
      and does not ask you to create an account.
    </p>
    <h2>Information this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      The site does not run an account system, and it does not set its own
      cookies or analytics. Your browser may still record the pages you visit in
      its own history. If you email
      <a href="mailto:bhavya.saggi@gmail.com">bhavya.saggi@gmail.com</a>, that
      message contains whatever you choose to send.
    </p>
    <h2>Generated documents</h2>
    <p>
      Invoices, receipts, slips, reports, and resumes are built from the text
      you type. That text is used to draw the PDF in your browser and is not
      sent to PDFvise.
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      PDFvise does not ask for personal information. It is a general-purpose PDF
      tool and is not directed at collecting information from children.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can go to
      <a href="mailto:bhavya.saggi@gmail.com">bhavya.saggi@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
